h1: "Date Difference Calculator"
quickAnswer: "To calculate the duration between two dates, pick your start date and end date, then select whether to include or exclude the final day. The calculator provides total calendar days, business days, weekends, weeks, and months. All calculations run client-side in UTC, preventing daylight saving time errors."
formula:
  title: "Date Span & Duration Formula"
  expression: "Duration = (End Date UTC ms - Start Date UTC ms) / 86,400,000 ms [± 1 day if inclusive]"
  explanation: "Calendar duration measures whole 24-hour UTC day intervals between two dates. When inclusive mode is selected, 1 day is added to count both boundary days. Business days evaluate each individual day in the span, tallying Mondays through Fridays and skipping weekend days."
workedExamples:
  - title: "Standard Work Month (Exclusive)"
    inputs:
      - "Start Date: October 1, 2026 (Thursday)"
      - "End Date: October 31, 2026 (Saturday)"
      - "Inclusive: No"
    steps:
      - "Compute calendar day interval: 30 days"
      - "Count Monday through Friday business days: 22 days"
      - "Count weekend days: 8 days (4 full weekends)"
    result: "30 Total Days (22 business days, 8 weekend days, 4 weeks and 2 days)"
  - title: "Inclusive Event Duration (Conference / Rental)"
    inputs:
      - "Start Date: November 1, 2026 (Sunday)"
      - "End Date: November 5, 2026 (Thursday)"
      - "Inclusive: Yes"
    steps:
      - "Compute raw interval: 4 days"
      - "Add 1 day for inclusive boundary: 5 days"
      - "Count working days (Mon-Thu): 4 business days, 1 weekend day (Sunday)"
    result: "5 Total Days (4 business days, 1 weekend day, 120 hours)"
  - title: "Cross-Quarter Duration Across Year Boundary"
    inputs:
      - "Start Date: December 15, 2025 (Monday)"
      - "End Date: March 15, 2026 (Sunday)"
      - "Inclusive: No"
    steps:
      - "Compute calendar days across year boundary: 90 days"
      - "Decompose into calendar months: exactly 3 months (0 remaining days)"
      - "Tally working days: 65 business days, 25 weekend days"
    result: "90 Total Days (3 months, 12 weeks and 6 days, 2,160 hours)"
commonMistakes:
  - title: "The Fencepost Problem (Inclusive vs. Exclusive)"
    description: "A hotel stay from Friday to Sunday is 2 nights (exclusive), but spans 3 calendar days (inclusive). Omitting clear boundary definitions causes booking discrepancies."
  - title: "Treating Business Days as an Approximate 5/7 Fraction"
    description: "Working days cannot be approximated as 5/7 of calendar days because weekend boundaries dramatically shift working day tallies in short ranges."
  - title: "Assuming Public Holidays Are Excluded"
    description: "The business day counter filters Saturdays and Sundays. Statutory national and provincial holidays vary by jurisdiction and are not automatically removed."
  - title: "Local Timezone Clock Shifts"
    description: "Calculating day differences using local midnight timestamps can introduce 23-hour or 25-hour errors during Daylight Saving Time switches."
sources:
  - name: "ISO 8601 Date and Time Standards"
