faqs:
  - q: "What is the difference between calendar days and business days?"
    a: "Calendar days include all 7 days of each week (Monday through Sunday), whereas business days count only standard working days from Monday through Friday, excluding weekend days."
  - q: "When should I check 'Include end date in the count'?"
    a: "Check this option if your activity or rental includes both boundary days. For example, a business conference taking place from Monday to Wednesday spans 3 full event days (inclusive), but is 2 days duration if measuring elapsed time (exclusive)."
  - q: "What happens if I enter an end date that occurs before the start date?"
    a: "The calculator detects reversed dates, swaps them to compute the positive span, and shows a helpful notice indicating that the dates were ordered automatically."
  - q: "How are leap years handled in multi-year durations?"
    a: "Calculations run on UTC midnight timestamps and evaluate each leap day (February 29th) that occurs within the range, ensuring that 366-day years are counted with complete precision. If a day does not exist in a month (for example the 31st), the last day of that month is used."
  - q: "Is any of my date data sent to an external server?"
    a: "No. All date arithmetic executes entirely in your web browser. No dates are transmitted or stored remotely."
  - q: "Can I use this tool to calculate business days for invoicing?"
    a: "Yes. The business day count gives the exact number of non-weekend days between the start date and the end date, ideal for net-30 payment or SLA tracking."
  - q: "How does the tool break down days into months and weeks?"
    a: "It computes whole elapsed calendar months first, then expresses the remainder in weeks and excess days, as well as providing absolute total days and hours."
